# "Turning it on" — what kind of video card is this?
#
# The emulator is a stock TMS9918A and masks register writes to 0-7, so this
# case proves the branch a stock card takes: the probe survives, nothing is
# claimed that is not there, and the three registers the attempt clobbered are
# put back. That last part is what makes the assertion worth making — the
# screen still works afterwards, which is exactly what goes wrong when a
# detection routine skips the restore.
#
# The F18A branches cannot be reached here. They need the real card.

console video
send \r

screen ^VIDEO: TMS9918A, NO F18A MODE\s*$
screen ^OK\s*$
